From 2a5d14df2f7e4ca1fd391acff0139baf225339da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:49:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] TFEL: consistent host and device annotations, device code of
 criteria and solvers

- definitions annotated as their declarations (clang CUDA refuses the
  mismatch accepted by nvcc): Barlat, Cazacu, Drucker, Mohr-Coulomb,
  Michel-Suquet, Rousselier, Gurson-Tvergaard-Needleman criteria, pi
  plane, nucleation models, DDIF2, Broyden, Levenberg-Marquardt, Powell,
  bissection and scalar Newton-Raphson solvers, PCW schemes
- C++11 attributes placed before the host and device annotations in DDIF2
- headers using TFEL_HOST_DEVICE include the TFEL configuration
- declarations of the Chu-Needleman strain based nucleation functions
  matching their definitions
- divergence of the GTN and Rousselier criteria and of the elastic
  prediction of the axial strain reported by an invalid value in device
  code instead of an exception
- Aitken acceleration, linear and cubic spline interpolations usable in
  device code
- the non linear solvers stop when the iteration counter reaches its
  maximum value, which allows aborting a resolution in device code
